<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76912" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλῐν-άγρετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be taken back</i> or <i>recalled</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ π. οὐδ᾽ ἀπατηλόν</span>
				ir<i>revocable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.526
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀάτη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					93
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότατα δ᾽ ἔχειν π. οὐκ ἔστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					29.28
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. αἰών, ἀρχή</span>, etc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				3.255
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.175
			</span></i>, al.; <i>recoverable</i>, of an element, <i><span class="en">
				Numen.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				15.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>retracting his words</i>, of the philosopher Arcesilaus,
				Id.ib.<i><span class="en">
				14.5
			</span></i>.</div>
